    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;4.06</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Summary of the main features of <em>CDKN2A</em>-related tumour predisposition syndrome</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "David A. Solomon",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 188.5pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"251\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Feature</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 278.5pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"371\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Syndrome characteristics</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 188.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"251\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Syndrome MIM number(s)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 278.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"371\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Depending on the tumour spectrum present in the kindred: 155601, 155755, 606719</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 188.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"251\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Associated malignant tumours</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 278.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"371\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cutaneous melanoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pleomorphic xanthoastrocytoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diffuse astrocytic glioma, IDH and histone H3 wildtype (ranging from histologically low-grade diffuse astrocytoma&ndash;like to high-grade glioblastoma-like tumours)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pancreatic carcinoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Oropharyngeal squamous cell carcinoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 188.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"251\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Associated benign tumours</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 278.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"371\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cutaneous atypical/dysplastic naevi (with elevated risk of progression to melanoma)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Neurofibroma-like nerve sheath tumours (with uncertain risk of progression to malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 188.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"251\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cancer-related inheritance</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 278.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"371\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Autosomal dominant</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 188.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"251\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Chromosome location</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 278.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"371\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CDKN2A</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (9p21.3)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 188.5pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"251\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Protein product&ndash;associated pathway</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 278.5pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"371\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">p16: negative regulator of CDK4 and CDK6 controlling cell-cycle progression</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">p14ARF: negative regulator of p53 signalling</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
